{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067268-ephemeral-entities-and-their-numina","id":1067268,"title":"Ephemeral Entities and their Numina","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-23T17:47:20-07:00","id":1067268,"title":"Ephemeral Entities and their Numina","content":"So I'm running a Mage game, and I have a player who has started to become very interested in Spirits and the Shadow. He's even grabbed a spirit familiar, and we've parsed that out for the most part. To this point, we haven't really done very much with the different invisible realms, but it's clear that that is about to change. So i've started brushing up on Spirits. I've picked up the Book of Spirits and have read through most of it and I feel like I'm starting to get a strong narrative sense of the Shadow and its inhabitants. But my mechanical understanding is a bit shaky.<br /> <br /> His Familiar is a water spirit, we've characterized it as a little blue dragon of sorts and he is affectionately called Blueshu (like from Mulan, but blue). <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Power: 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resistance: 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Finesse: 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Corpus: 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willpower: 6 </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiative: 6 </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Defense: 4 </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed: 9 (Species factor 3 on land, 8 in water?)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Size: 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Language: Harsh, strange tongue of the Shadow-World</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Influence: Water \u2022\u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Manifestations: Twilight Form, Gateway, Materialize, Familiar</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Numina: Blast<br /> <br /> So one of my main hangups is spirits in twilight. They can't really interact with the material world in twilight, they just pass right through it. So this brings up a few questions: Can the Mage cast spells through the Familiar in twilight to affect the material world? My gut says no, I feel like blueshu would have to use the Materialize Manifestation to do that. And what about Numina? Can the spirit use Numina in Twilight to manipulate and affect the material world?<br /> <br /> I suppose these questions apply to the other ephemeral creatures as well, but for now my main focus is on the Spirits.<br /> <br /> Thanks for any/all comments and suggestions! </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:52:08-07:00","id":1067269,"title":"","content":"The mage can cast spells on anything they can perceive. Beings in Twilight still perceive the physical world, even if they can't interact with it. There's nothing stopping the mage from casting spells that affect physical subjects through their familiar. They just need to use the right Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:59:40-07:00","id":1067270,"title":"","content":"I love Blast. This sucker has a 6 die Lethal attack with a range of 20 yards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mofous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067268-ephemeral-entities-and-their-numina#post1067268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one of my main hangups is spirits in twilight. They can't really interact with the material world in twilight, they just pass right through it. So this brings up a few questions: Can the Mage cast spells through the Familiar in twilight to affect the material world? My gut says no, I feel like blueshu would have to use the Materialize Manifestation to do that. And what about Numina? Can the spirit use Numina in Twilight to manipulate and affect the material world?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the spell is cast at Sensory Range, you should be able to, as entities in Twilight can see entities not in Twilight. I believe you need another Reach to cast through a Familiar but that would be under the Familiar Merit or Condition.<br /> <br /> Generally you need to be in the same state to use Numina on others. So you can't use Blast from a Twilight state to a mortal not in Twilight. There's an exception in Left-Handed Spanner, however, which requires the spirit to just superimpose its in-Twilight form over the targeted object. Outside of that I think you could justify Firestarter and Telekinesis working from Twilight, as they can be used when Reaching from across the Gauntlet so you probably don't need to physically be there, along with a few other Numina.[/QUOTE]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T18:06:18-07:00","id":1067274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mofous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067268-ephemeral-entities-and-their-numina#post1067268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And what about Numina? Can the spirit use Numina in Twilight to manipulate and affect the material world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely a spirit can use numina while in twilight to affect the material world. Numina and influences are how ephemeral beings in the Twilight Form manifestation affect the physical world. So that familiar you have statted can cause damaging sprays of water (the type of blast that seems appropriate for a water spirit) that affect things in the material world while in twilight form by spending essence to use blast. <br /> <br /> A numina that demonstrates this well is Sign. If a spirit had to Materialize to use the numina it could just physically interact and not need the numina.<br /> <br /> Noticing a lack of a ban/bane. You should fix that. An idea may be requiring proximity of water with the Open condition to use its numina (thematic and not overly burdensome because it can strengthen Resonant water with its influence). Additionally that makes growth as a spirit interesting with that limitation and encourages playing to the spirit's strength by staying near areas with Resonant water (rivers, lakes, oceans, ect...), and thus adds flavor to in game behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-23-2017, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:18:15-07:00","id":1067665,"title":"","content":"Okay, <br /> So the Twilight Form Manifestation is sort of a static Manifestation that is always on. So if they're in twilight they can use their Numina and the Mage can cast his spells? The Spirit doesn't have to do an additional Manifestation to use those powers (unless otherwise stated)? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067268-ephemeral-entities-and-their-numina?p=1067274#post1067274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noticing a lack of a ban/bane. You should fix that. An idea may be requiring proximity of water with the Open condition to use its numina (thematic and not overly burdensome because it can strengthen Resonant water with its influence). Additionally that makes growth as a spirit interesting with that limitation and encourages playing to the spirit's strength by staying near areas with Resonant water (rivers, lakes, oceans, ect...), and thus adds flavor to in game behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I am missing the ban/bane and I'll definitely consider that idea. Thank you! <br /> Since we are new to the whole Shadow/Spirit thing, I haven't quite figured bans/banes out. I understand the concept, but have not yet been able to create anything that I feel is working. So the Familiar is currently strolling around without any real flaws. If anyone can point me in a direction regarding bans/banes inspiration, I would certainly appreciate it :P <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:45:35-07:00","id":1067685,"title":"","content":"Ban: When presented with something valuable the dragon has to take it to its underwater hoard immediately. (Availability Rating 2 or higher).<br /> <br /> Bane: A piece of wood that saved a drowning person.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, if in Twilight the spirit can use its powers or be cast through by the Mage without further Manifestations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T12:29:39-07:00","id":1067736,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me it may be fun to brainstorm bans and banes for this spirit, and that could be helpful.<br /> <br /> Bane: Broken Pearls (as symbols of water, their broken form could represent breaking water, though this is a bit too rare for a rank 2 spirit)<br /> <br /> Ban: Must open a Gate within water during a <a href=\"http://oceanservice.noaa.gov/facts/springtide.html\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;spring tide&quot;</a>. (Using Influence to make it Open as needed)<br /> <br /> Bane: Salt (Appropriate if a fresh water spring was its original source for Essence)<br /> <br /> Ban: Must drown one person a year.<br /> <br /> Bane: Pumice.<br /> <br /> Ban: Must Materialize is exposed to Ice (Using Influence to make it Open as needed).<br /> <br /> Bane: Fire larger than it (Evaporates into steam, since it is so little)<br /> <br /> Ban: Must obey holder of a particular pearl ring (Who happens to be the PCs ancestor)<br /> <br /> Bane: An item with Chinese character \u65f1 h\u00e0n, meaning drought, on it.<br /> <br /> Ban: Must Blast at least once if caught in a rainstorm.<br /> <br /> Bane:Any solid object that isn't wet.<br /> <br /> Ban: Must always Materialize if caught in a rainstorm. (Using Influence to make it Open as needed)<br /> <br /> Bane: A drinking cup or bowl<br /> <br /> Ban: Must Always open a Gate if caught in a rainstorm. (Using Influence to make it Open as needed)<br /> <br /> ====<br /> <br /> Don't forget Banes are solid to ephemeral beings in Twilight Form. Also it only take Spirit 1, Know Spirit to know what its bane/ban is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-24-2017, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T13:08:35-07:00","id":1067754,"title":"","content":"Guidelines for a Rank 2 entity:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ban: Rank 2 and 3 entities have moderate bans that curtail the<br /> creature\u2019s activities in a more serious way than mere distraction.<br /> The murderous spirit of a car that has run down multiple people<br /> loses all Willpower if it doesn\u2019t kill one person a month. A ghost<br /> must immediately dematerialize when it hears the sound of a cat. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bane: Rank 2 and 3 spirits have difficult to obtain but still \u201cnatural\u201d<br /> banes. A wild-wood spirit must be killed by a sharpened stake<br /> made of pine. A goetic entity of self-loathing is vulnerable to<br /> any mirror that it has seen its reflection in. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T13:57:15-07:00","id":1067774,"title":"","content":"Okay, awesome. <br /> Keeping the rules <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> kindly posted in mind, I really enjoy the idea of this little dragon having to take valuable items that are offered to him and stash them deep down in the Mississippi River (where he derived from) or else lose all of his Willpower. <br /> <br /> But if the Bane has to be difficult to obtain, maybe we could run with salt, but it has to be the salt that is found at the very bottom of the river. So you're going to have to go out of your way to actually acquire it. Do you think that works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:16:12-07:00","id":1067783,"title":"","content":"Going by the example from the book for the wild-wood spirit that must be killed by a sharpened stake made of pine it's not unreasonable, but does salt accumulate at the bottom of rivers? I'd assume it would be dissolved into the water rendering that particular task all but impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T15:15:24-07:00","id":1067808,"title":"","content":"Could just be a rock from the bottom of the river he came from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T16:54:47-07:00","id":1067845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067268-ephemeral-entities-and-their-numina?p=1067783#post1067783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going by the example from the book for the wild-wood spirit that must be killed by a sharpened stake made of pine it's not unreasonable, but does salt accumulate at the bottom of rivers? I'd assume it would be dissolved into the water rendering that particular task all but impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're probably right. I did a quick google search and made some inaccurate assumptions without doing research before posting. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067268-ephemeral-entities-and-their-numina?p=1067808#post1067808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could just be a rock from the bottom of the river he came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like a reasonable substitution that is a million times more achievable.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T08:52:45-07:00","id":1068020,"title":"","content":"Also, don't forget any rank 4 or higher spirit's natural attacks act as banes, as any being with Honorary Rank (*cough*Some Uratha*cough* and Spirit adepts). <br /> <br /> Also the rock from the bottom of the Missippi is a great idea, but what adds to its symbolic power over water? Maybe a rock or gravel from a levy would be better? The Missippi river has a lot of levies to control its flooding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-25-2017, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T09:16:19-07:00","id":1068023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067268-ephemeral-entities-and-their-numina?p=1068020#post1068020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the rock from the bottom of the Missippi is a great idea, but what adds to its symbolic power over water? Maybe a rock or gravel from a levy would be better? The Missippi river has a lot of levies to control its flooding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that, in addition to acting as a floor-like barrier for the river, since the spirit takes the form of a dragon it can likely fly, so it probably was representative of some waves or rapids, and there would probably be a 'power' to it too since a dragon is symbolic of power, even if small, and the lowest and most impenetrable part of the river would be anathema to it.<br /> <br /> I pondered about something where the Mississippi ends, like water for the Atlantic, but a rock is, plainly, easier and just as uncommon to find while not being impossible to justify an antagonist having.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T17:23:47-07:00","id":1068487,"title":"","content":"Thank you for all of the help guys! I truly appreciate it. I'm sure I'll be back asking questions about these ephemeral creatures again shortly. But for the time being I feel like I have a stronger grasp of the mechanics. <br /> <br /> Also, I think I've settled on:<br /> Ban: Blueshu must take any valuable item (availability rating 2 or higher) offered to him down into the Mississippi River. <br /> Bane: Blueshu is vulnerable to water gathered from the Gulf of Mexico, where the Mississippi ends (the Gulf is only 2 or 3 hours from where the chronicle is set).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T19:23:01-07:00","id":1068511,"title":"","content":"What rank is your familiar? The power spread implies rank 1, but the influence of 2 says rank 2. The old ed 1 rule that let familiars flout spirit rules (which weren't firmed up when those familiar rules were written) and have 2 dots of influence at rank 1 doesn't apply in 2ed, so I would drop the influence to 1, or increase his stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T20:31:19-07:00","id":1068529,"title":"","content":"Good eye, it would just need another Attribute dot to fit in Rank 2. It would also have one more Manifestation or Numina. Two if you don't want to count Familiar.<br /> <br /> Maybe it was designed Rank 1, sacrificed some Numina for Influence, breaking the Rank limit for Influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T07:02:20-07:00","id":1068649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067268-ephemeral-entities-and-their-numina?p=1068529#post1068529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it was designed Rank 1, sacrificed some Numina for Influence, breaking the Rank limit for Influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right. We removed a Numina to increase the Influence and Materialize Manifestion. We dropped that Manifestation though, given the rule clarification you guys provided, and pushed in the Numina Regenerate.<br /> <br /> I had a momentary lapse in memory about the Rank though while we were discussing the Ban/Bane and started assuming it was Rank 2. So there may need to be a minor adjustment there. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar532_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"532\" data-vbnamecard=\"532\">Newes</a> Thanks for jogging me back to reality.<br /> <br /> I think I'm okay with the Ban, but maybe the Bane should be adjusted to something slightly easier to obtain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T07:48:51-07:00","id":1068665,"title":"","content":"Probably. Salt is a very common Bane for Rank 1 entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}